extends ../../../layouts/master.pug

block title
  title NBC - Associate of Arts in Ministry

block header
  include ../../../components/header.pug

block content
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.nav-breadcrums.bg-gray-100
      .container
        .breadcrumb
          ul
            li.home
              a(href='/index-4.html') Home
            li
              a(href='/programs/') Programs
            li
              span A.A. in Ministry
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.banner-head-image(style='background: url(/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_332409626.jpeg); background-size: cover; background-position: center bottom;')
      .container
        .text-center
          h1.text-heading-1.color-white.mt-30
            | Associate of Arts in Ministry
  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h2#overview.text-heading-4 Overview
            p.text-body-text
              | The Associate of Arts in Ministry (A.A. Min.) degree is designed for persons who wish to gain ministry skills and knowledge in order to serve as lay workers in churches or Christian organizations. The degree is based on a strong general studies component and introductory studies in Bible, theology, and ministry principles. While not providing all the competencies for completion of ordination education requirements in the Church of the Nazarene, the program gives foundational knowledge and skills for lay contribution to the work of the church either as volunteers or as paid staff members. Persons who desire to complete ordination requirements may do so by taking approximately eleven additional courses.
        .row
          .col-lg-12
            .row
              .col-lg-6
                h2#majors.text-heading-4.mt-30 Degree Requirements
                p.text-body-text
                  | All associate programs with a specialization in ministry contain the following degree requirements:
                ul
                  li  Completion of a minimum of 64 semester hours.
                  li At least 32 semester hours in residence–with at least 16 of the final 32 hours in residence. Online classes are considered “in residence.”
                  li  A cumulative GPA of at least 2.0 (on a 4.0 scale).
                  li Completion of the required hours in the following areas:
                    ul
                      li General Education
                      li Bible and Theology
                      li Major Concentration
                  li Completion of NBC Experience.
                  li College indebtedness paid in full.

              .col-lg-6.d-flex.justify-content-center.flex-column
                img.img-responsive.bdr-10.mt-10.ml-10(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_523952347.jpeg', alt='Agon')

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h3.text-heading-3.mb-20.color-green-900.text-center Core Requirements and Objectives
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h4.text-heading-5.mb-20.text-center General Education Core
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th Course
                  th Course Description
                  th Hours
              tbody
                +CourseTableRow('ENG-1013', 'English Composition I', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('ENG-1023', 'English Composition II', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('GEN-1003', 'Lifelong Learning Skills', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('HIS-2023', 'Western World/Emerging Modern Society', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('MTH-1003', 'General Mathematics', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('PSY-1013', 'Introduction to Psychology', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('SCI-2013', 'General Physical Science', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('SPE-1003', 'Principles of Public Speaking', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('THE-3013', 'Introduction to Christian Thought', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('', 'General Studies Elective', '1')
              tfoot
                tr
                  td
                  td
                  td
                    strong 28 hours

        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h4.text-heading-5.mb-20.text-center Bible and Theology Core
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th Course
                  th Course Description
                  th Hours
              tbody
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-1013', 'Introduction to the Old Testament', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-1023', 'Introduction to the New Testament', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-2003', 'Biblical Interpretation', '3')
              tfoot
                tr
                  td 
                  td 
                  td 
                    strong 9 hours

        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h3.text-heading-4.mb-20 Concentrations
            p.text-body-text The student must select one of the following concentrations to complete the hours required for an Associate of Arts degree:
            ul
              li
                a(href='/concentrations/christian-educational-ministries/') Christian Educational Ministries
              li
                a(href='/concentrations/church-ministries/') Church Ministries
              li
                a(href='/concentrations/hispanic-pastoral-ministries/') Hispanic Pastoral Ministries
